{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/13714-can-sin-eater-charms-get-stronger-from-other-supenaturals","id":13714,"title":"Can Sin eater charms get stronger from other supenaturals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-18T18:00:19-08:00","id":13714,"title":"Can Sin eater charms get stronger from other supenaturals","content":"For instance if a sin eater gets help from a changeling into making a tattoo charm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T19:28:12-08:00","id":13738,"title":"","content":"No, they cannot. That's not how mementos work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T01:51:45-08:00","id":13871,"title":"","content":"No, other supernaturals cannot enhance a charm, could a supernatural make a charm another kind of magic item? There's no rule against it except for the possibility that the ST might hit you with newspaper for suggesting it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now making a charm a relic wouldn't work because the relic creator merit requires that the relic creator create the relic themselves, and a demon couldn't make a gadget out of a charm because gadgets are specifically incompatible with other forms of magic item, but I can't think of any specific rule barring changeling tokens, or werewolf fetishes or possessed items, or mage imbued or enhanced items.<br /> <br /> Perhaps WW thought the idea of a relic token fetish fetter imbued item was just so silly they didn't need to, I don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T07:11:06-08:00","id":14681,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with StSword. I can see a fetter/charm being an important component or vessel for a fetish, but at that point it would become a fetish, not a charm anymore.<br /> Could make for interesting conflict, if the different groups can make their own items out of other people's, but the short answer seems to be &quot;no&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>ST/DM for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCfFy7kNgMvxIR1qdzT8PzEg\" target=\"_blank\">Dice Alternatives</a><br /> Playing: <a href=\"http://causality-and-consequences.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DtD: Causality and Consequence</a><br /> Off-Season: <a href=\"http://lifelong-educations.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">M:tAw- Lifelong Education</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/667-abenniton","name":"ABenniton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar667_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T15:18:40-08:00","id":14904,"title":"","content":"thanks all i needed to know","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T15:49:46-08:00","id":14923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/13714-can-sin-eater-charms-get-stronger-from-other-supenaturals?p=13871#post13871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now making a charm a relic wouldn't work because the relic creator merit requires that the relic creator create the relic themselves, and a demon couldn't make a gadget out of a charm because gadgets are specifically incompatible with other forms of magic item, but I can't think of any specific rule barring changeling tokens, or werewolf fetishes or possessed items, or mage imbued or enhanced items.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;It should also be noted that tokens resist any sort of alteration to their form from outside sources. A mage who uses magic to change a token's shape or a werewolf who attempts to dedicate a token to her body may find that they have accidentally destroyed the token\u2026 or increased the power of its drawback.&quot;<br /> <br /> Fetishes require the object to resonate with the spirit(s)'s nature and fetters need to be made out of an anchor, either of which magical alteration might interfere with.<br /> <br /> Don't recall anything concerning the particulars of enchantment or imbuement via Awakened magic being thrown off unless one counts the vague possibility of a Fate-conditional duration for Imbue Item.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T02:25:35-08:00","id":15259,"title":"","content":"Now one item combination I find might make a good storyhook would be a sin-eater item's spirit awakening, perhaps the ordeal that made it appropriate for a sin-eater item made it a spirit of death as well as whatever it was originally. Imagine the sin-eater's confusion over one of their items developing a mind of its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T09:05:23-08:00","id":15409,"title":"","content":"Also, I'd think <i>most</i> sin-eater items have enough emotion invested in them to also be Mummy Vestiges. Just not relics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T00:32:53-08:00","id":16982,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/13714-can-sin-eater-charms-get-stronger-from-other-supenaturals?p=15409#post15409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'd think <i>most</i> sin-eater items have enough emotion invested in them to also be Mummy Vestiges. Just not relics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitional concerns may make even that unlikely:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mummy Lexicon, &quot;vestige&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A vessel containing only pure/unrefined Sekhem and <b>bearing no mystical properties</b>, but holding a great deal of emotional or spiritual value to one or more earth-bound souls.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T10:08:24-08:00","id":24411,"title":"","content":"*Groans a bit as he finds a seat, and glances up through the thread idly, nodding at comments here and there.*<br /> <br /> Purely speculation, my dear lads and ladies, but I was under the impression that Mage could break any other game they involved themselves, in were we to imagine this or that in terms of mechanics. Considering the fact that at certain power levels, (many different ones, in fact) of Death could somehow enhance a Charm, Momento; what-have-you. I believe a friend of mine told me about one of the eldest books in the Mage collection had mechanics for creating templates? (And I believe, at the very least, it only requires a Master of each Arcana to create their own spells, yes?)<br /> <br /> *he winces, as though the talk of mechanics pains him*<br /> <br /> It's obvious that the original intent behind the cookie-cutter design of the NWoD books was to make them more interchangeable, and multi-genre-friendly; and at the same time, make sure items, powers, castes and character templates to remain a short, almost-hugging distance. But the mechanics are something that grind my gears the wrong way.<br /> <br /> I offer to you, to consider the fluff in all this: is it possible? Very. Is it likely? Not really, unless you have a player-base that would suggest someone willing to betray the secrets and oaths and such that some/most of the different templates must swear to be in whatever collectives they maintain. And forgive me for venturing to the foyer just overlooking Gentleman Lake a moment to be a -touch- rude about the entire idea: seeking out more powerful items beyond what the books clearly lay out, is a bit crass. You owe it to yourself as a classy individual, and a being a Gentleman or Lady to play for the story, and be willing to struggle for what you wish to obtain. (Which should be goals and good story: not material.) Let the Storyteller award you Shiny Bits.<br /> <br /> What's stronger than a big stick? Having lots of friends with sticks. *He nods a bit sagely* Making lots of friends that value you will always be more &quot;powerful&quot; than any item, spell, or trick. What does having the Shiniest Bit usually get you? Jealous admirers who will kick your false teeth in, via curb-stomp: and if your Storyteller doesn't place those types of characters into your Chronicle; he/she is either being too kind, or is lulling you into a false sense of Macho Man Randy Savage.<br /> <br /> *he sips his tea quietly*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1219-shake","name":"Shake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}